# mbsync (isync) configuration for topo.tw
# Mirrors the IMAP account defined in ~/.muttrc (muttrc.topo)
#
# Usage:
#   mbsync topo        # sync the whole account
#   mbsync topo-fetch  # INBOX only, read-only pull (goimapnotify hook)
#   mbsync -a          # every channel, i.e. topo + a redundant topo-fetch
#   mbsync -l topo     # list-only: show which folders would sync
#
# Local maildir lives under ~/Maildir, INBOX in ~/Maildir/INBOX (same as on v)
#
# Login note: muttrc's imaps://pham@mail.topo.tw:993 means the LOGIN user is
# "pham" on host mail.topo.tw; "pham@mail.topo.tw" is only the `pass` entry name.

IMAPAccount topo
Host mail.topo.tw
Port 993
User pham
PassCmd "pass mail/pham@mail.topo.tw"
TLSType IMAPS
CertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt

IMAPStore topo-remote
Account topo

MaildirStore topo-local
SubFolders Verbatim
Inbox ~/Maildir/INBOX
Path ~/Maildir/

Channel topo
Far :topo-remote:
Near :topo-local:
# Sync every folder. On v, INBOX is ~/Maildir/INBOX (Dovecot Maildir, fs layout).
# To skip scratch folders, append e.g.: !"tmp" !"test" !"zl*"
Patterns *
Create Both
Expunge Both
SyncState *

# INBOX-only pull used by the goimapnotify onNewMail hook: it just needs the
# new message on disk so the hook can read its Subject header, so nothing is
# ever pushed or expunged upstream. Shares ~/Maildir/INBOX/.mbsyncstate with "topo"
# (SyncState lives with the mailbox, not the channel), so the two stay in step.
Channel topo-fetch
Far :topo-remote:
Near :topo-local:
Patterns "INBOX"
Sync Pull
Create Near
Expunge None
SyncState *
